cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Security Core FFI: Nucleu de Securitate Criptografic Multi-Limbaj"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/CiprianStefanPlesca/security-core-ffi"
abstract: >
  A memory-safe cryptographic security core (AES-256-GCM) written in Rust,
  compiled as a dynamic library and exposed through an extern "C" (FFI)
  interface, enabling direct integration into C++, Python, Node.js, and
  WebAssembly (browser/Next.js), without duplicating the encryption logic
  for each platform.
authors:
  - family-names: "Pleșca"
    given-names: "Ciprian Ștefan"
    affiliation: "Independent author"
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - rust
  - ffi
  - aes-gcm
  - security
  - cross-language
  - foreign-function-interface
  - webassembly
  - wasm-bindgen
  - nextjs
